Usage: keymaerax-core [setup|prove|parse|bparse|convert|grade] [options] <args>...

  -h, --help               Show this usage information.
  --launch                 Use present JVM instead of launching one with a
                           bigger stack.
  --debug <value>          Enable/disable debug mode with exhaustive messages.
  --jlink path/to/jlinkNativeLib
                           Path to Mathematica J/Link library directory.
  --jlinkinterface <format>
                           Format for sending commands to Mathematica. Possible
                           values: String (more robust), Expr (supports larger
                           queries).
  --jlinktcpip <bool>      Whether to connect to Mathematica with process
                           communication or over TCP/IP (more robust). Default:
                           false (unless configured in keymaerax.conf)
  --lax <value>            true: Use lax mode with more flexible parser,
                           printer, prover. false: Use strict mode with no
                           flexibility in prover.
  --mathkernel MathKernel(.exe)
                           Path to Mathematica kernel executable.
  --open <value>
  --parallelqe <bool>      Whether to attempt multiple QE alternatives in
                           parallel. Default: false (unless configured in
                           keymaerax.conf)
  --qemethod <method>      Quantifier elimination method to use. Possible
                           values: Reduce (solves equations and eliminates
                           quantifiers), Resolve (eliminates quantifiers).
  --tool <name>            Choose which tool to use for real arithmetic.
                           Possible values: Mathematica, WolframEngine,
                           WolframScript, Z3.
  --z3path path/to/z3      Path to Z3 executable.

Command: setup
Initialize the configuration and lemma cache.

Command: prove [options] <in> [<out>]
Run prover on given archive of models or proofs.
  <in>                     Input archive file(s) (either a specific file or a
                           wildcard, e.g. *.kyx).
  <out>                    Output proof file (defaults to input file with .kyp
                           suffix).
  --pt-out <file>          Output proof term s-expression into a file.
  --conjecture <file>      Conjecture file to replace the model in the input
                           file with (either a specific file or a wildcard, e.g.
                           *.kyx).
  --tactic <file|tactic>   Either a file containing a tactic, or a parseable
                           tactic. Used to prove the entry/entries in the input
                           or conjecture file.
  --tactic-name <name>     Which of the tactics in the input file to use
                           (default: check all, falling back to auto if no
                           tactic is listed). Only used if no tactic is
                           specified.
  --timeout <duration>     How long to try proving before giving up. Format:
                           "<length><unit>" or "Inf". Available units: d (day),
                           h (hour), m (minute), s (second), ms (millisecond).
                           Default: Inf.
  --verbose                Print verbose proof information.
  --statistics <format>    How to print proof statistics. Possible values: Csv,
                           ArchNlnCsv, ArchHstpCsv. Default: Csv.

Command: parse <in>
Return error code 0 if the given model file parses.
  <in>                     Input file.

Command: bparse <in>
Return error code 0 if given bellerophon tactic file parses.
  <in>                     Input file.

Command: convert <conversion> <in> [<out>]
Model conversions.
  <conversion>             Conversion to perform. Possible values: KyxToMat,
                           SmtToMat, KyxToSmt, SmtToKyx, StripHints.
  <in>                     Input file.
  <out>                    Output file.

Command: grade [options] <in> [<out>]

  <in>                     File to grade.
  <out>                    Output directory for answer files.
  --export-answers         Export answers to text files instead of grading.
  --skip-on-parse-error    Skip grading on parse errors.
